ved from di̇̀dis (“big, large”) + -elis, with further etymology of the first component uncertain. Possibly from Proto-Indo-European *deyh₂-dʰe-, from *deyh₂- (“to shine”), with semantic shift \"shining\" > \"visible\" > \"large\"; in this case, related to Homeric Greek δέατο (déato, “[he/she/it] showed themselves”), δῆλος (dêlos, “visible”), Vedic Sanskrit दीदाय (dīdā́ya, “[he/she/it] shines”), दीप् (dīp, “to blaze, glow”), and see the latter for more.\nWindekens tentatively compares it with Ancient Greek Τῑτᾱ́ν (Tītā́n, “titan”) (possibly of Anatolian origin).\nCognate with Latvian dižs, dideļš.", "etymology_templates": [{"name": "affix", "args": {"1": "lt", "2": "dìdis", "t1": "big, large", "3": "-elis"}, "expansion": "di̇̀dis (“big, large”) + -elis"}, {"name": "der", "args": {"1": "lt", "2": "ine-pro", "3": "", "4": "*deyh₂-dʰe-"}, "expansion": "Proto-Indo-European *deyh₂-dʰe-"}, {"name": "cog", "args": {"1": "sa-ved", "2": "दीदाय", "tr": "dīdā́ya", "3": "", "4": "􂀿he/she/it􂁀 shines"}, "expansion": "Vedic Sanskrit दीदाय (dīdā́ya, “[he/she/it] shines”)"}, {"name": "cog", "args": {"1": "grc", "2": "Τῑτᾱ́ν", "3": "", "4": "titan"}, "expansion": "Ancient Greek Τῑτᾱ́ν (Tītā́n, “titan”)"}, {"name": "cog", "args": {"1": "lv", "2": "dižs"}, "expansion": "Latvian dižs"}], "sounds": [{"ipa": "[ˈdʲɪdʲɛlʲɪs]"}, {"rhymes": "-ɪdʲɛlʲɪs"}], "hyphenation": ["di̇̀‧de‧lis"], "hyphenations": [{"parts": ["di̇̀‧de‧lis"]}], "word": "didelis", "lang": "Lithuanian", "lang_code": "lt"}